// XFAIL: RT-397: a generic impl's associated type is never checked against the trait's bound on it: `trait H { type Out: Tr<i64>; }` and `impl<T> H for B<T> { type Out = W; }`, where W has only Tr<i32>, is accepted (rustc E0277, `W: Tr<i64>` is not satisfied) (0.30.2)
// From the review of g302oblig-m2 (form f271l). Since v0.30.1 at least;
// the release build the same. rustc E0277 at `type Out = W` (the rustc
// twin of this file). The same bound in an impl without type parameters
// is checked. Sub-forms: rt_397b (the bound names Self, `Out: Tr<Self>`),
// rt_397c (the same used: a generic body calls the impl that is not
// there, and runs Tr<B<i64>>'s g for a B<i32>). RT-398 is the opposite
// error (a bound that holds refused).
// ERROR: line 34
// ERROR-COUNT: 1
trait Tr<U> {
    fn g(&self) -> i64;
}

trait H {
    type Out: Tr<i64>;
}

struct W {
    r: i64,
}

struct B<T> {
    t: T,
}

impl Tr<i32> for W {
    fn g(&self) -> i64 {
        9
    }
}

impl<T> H for B<T> {
    type Out = W;
}

fn main() {
    println("{}", 1);
}
